programs.mechanism_summary:
There is no single disease model. Traditional framings are kosha/prana imbalance. Contemporary framings are layered:
- breath and relaxation shift autonomic balance toward parasympathetic/vagal tone and lower HPA reactivity;
- postures retrain musculoskeletal and sensorimotor function;
- mindful movement builds interoception and acceptance and reduces catastrophizing;
- in TCTSY, trauma is held in the body as dysregulated arousal and loss of agency, and is restored through choice-based embodied practice.

Practice is tailored to each condition, but the model is shared and transdiagnostic.
